//! The crate is `no_std` compatible: it uses only `core` and allocates nothing.
//! The `no_std` attribute is gated on `not(test)` only because the libtest
//! harness itself requires `std`; downstream builds are unaffected, since
//! `cfg(test)` is never set for dependencies.

// `not(test)` is required by the unit tests below, which link the std-based
// test harness. Consumers still get a `no_std` crate.
